    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # 30040-30042: Vgs sigmoid gate to suppress NN correction below a threshold.
    #
    # Root-cause diagnosis: at low Vgs the NN produces a Gm bump because
    #   term B = Iphys * g_Vds * sech²(NN) * dNN/dVgs  is non-zero even
    #   when Iphys ≈ 0 (the NN gradient bleeds from the high-Vgs region).
    # Fix: multiply by g_Vgs = sigmoid((Vgs - vgs_thr) / vgs_tau)
    #   so the correction → 0 below the threshold → dIds/dVgs is clean there.
    #
    # Ids = Iphys * (1 + alpha_max * g_Vds * g_Vgs * tanh(NN))
    #
    # knee_vgs_thr ∈ (-3.0, -0.5) V  [linear Optuna sampling in physical V domain]
    # knee_vgs_tau ∈ (0.05,  2.0) V  [log Optuna sampling, controls gate sharpness]
    #
    # Best visual configs from previous sweeps: 30022/30032 (MSE + element-wise-soft).
    # These tests add the Vgs gate to the same combinations.
    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

    # ── 30040: MSELoss, no GM, Vgs gate sampled ───────────────────────────────────
