    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # 30043 – 30046 : Functional fix for low-Vgs noise fitting
    # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    # Root-cause analysis for the visual bumps/dips at low Vgs despite small NMSE:
    #   - NMSE is variance-weighted ⇒ dominated by high-Vgs / high-Ids samples.
    #     A 50 mA bump at low Vgs is invisible to the loss (≈0.06 % of one sample).
    #   - At low Vgs the measurement noise floor (~5–20 mA) is the *signal*,
    #     so the NN ends up fitting noise → bumps and dips.
    #
    # Two opt-in mechanisms (both default to OFF if not in general_opts):
    #
    #   knee_criterion = "FlooredRelativeMSELoss"
    #     L = mean( (pred-true)² / (|true| + floor)² )
    #     • floor (Amps) = "knee_floor_eps" in general_opts (scalar or (lo,hi))
    #     • Equal weight per decade for |Ids| >> floor → low-Vgs region is
    #       actually penalised; floor prevents blow-up below noise level.
    #
    #   low_ids_mask = threshold (Amps) or (lo, hi) tuple
    #     • Drops training samples where |Ids| < threshold.
    #     • Removes noise-dominated samples ⇒ NN no longer learns to fit
    #       them ⇒ physics term smoothly extrapolates Ids≈0 below threshold.
    #     • Validation set is untouched → reported NMSE stays comparable.
    #
    # All four spaces use the 30041 baseline (best so far: NMSE = 6.05e-4) and
    # toggle one or both new mechanisms.
